        "problem": "$\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x{sin}^{2}\u2061x}=$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we rewrite the numerator using $1-{cos}^{2}\u2061x={sin}^{2}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x{sin}^{2}\u2061x}=\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x{sin}^{2}\u2061x}\n$$\n\nNext, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x{sin}^{2}\u2061x} & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot {sin}^{2}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot \\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x{sin}^{2}\u2061x}=\\operatorname{sec}\u2061x.\n$$",
